    "question": {
      ":question/id": "12dbf628-215e-5f35-ab9e-dc556eaef7ad",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "\n\n$$\n\\int 5 xe^{3 x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n\n",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 5 xe^{3 x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =5 x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=5 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =e^{3 x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{e^{3 x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 5 x\\cdot e^{3 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5 x\\cdot \\frac{e^{3 x}}{3}-\\int \\frac{e^{3 x}}{3}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5 xe^{3 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 5 xe^{3 x}-\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot \\int e^{3 x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 5 xe^{3 x}-\\frac{5}{9}\\cdot e^{3 x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5 xe^{3 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\frac{5 x e^{3 x}}{3} - \\frac{5 e^{3 x}}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
