      ":question/id": "41281288-562a-52cd-8a2f-d770eb329551",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "\n\n$$\n\\int 4 xe^{4 x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n\n",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 4 xe^{4 x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =4 x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=4 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =e^{4 x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{e^{4 x}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 4 x\\cdot e^{4 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4 x\\cdot \\frac{e^{4 x}}{4}-\\int \\frac{e^{4 x}}{4}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4 xe^{4 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 xe^{4 x}-\\int e^{4 x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 xe^{4 x}-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot e^{4 x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4 xe^{4 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =x e^{4 x} - \\frac{e^{4 x}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
