      ":question/problem": "Calculate \n\n$$\n\\int 2 xe^{- 6 x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2 xe^{- 6 x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =2 x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =e^{- 6 x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=- \\frac{e^{- 6 x}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2 x\\cdot e^{- 6 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2 x\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{e^{- 6 x}}{6}\\right)-\\int \\left(- \\frac{e^{- 6 x}}{6}\\right)\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =- \\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 2 xe^{- 6 x}+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\int e^{- 6 x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2 xe^{- 6 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =- \\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 2 xe^{- 6 x}+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\int e^{- 6 x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =- \\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 2 xe^{- 6 x}-\\frac{1}{18}\\cdot e^{- 6 x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2 xe^{- 6 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =-\\frac{x e^{- 6 x}}{3} - \\frac{e^{- 6 x}}{18}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
