      "id": "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948",
      "title": "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1920a6e8-43b8-5c51-80e7-c18431876539",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral \n\n$$\n\\int (x + 3)e^{x - 5}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x + 3)e^{x - 5}\\,\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =x + 3\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =e^{x - 5}\\, & ⟹\\,v=e^{x - 5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x + 3)\\cdot e^{x - 5}\\,\\text{d}x & =(x + 3)\\cdot e^{x - 5}-\\int e^{x - 5}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x + 3)e^{x - 5}\\,\\text{d}x & =(x + 3)e^{x - 5}-\\int e^{x - 5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x + 3)e^{x - 5}-e^{x - 5}+C \\\\  & =(x + 2)e^{x - 5}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x + 3)e^{x - 5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\left(x + 2\\right)e^{x - 5}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
